### TECHNOLOGY DOMAIN
1. **Visual Programming & Educational Animation** – Master block-based coding (Scratch) and visual storytelling tools (Pictobox) for interactive explainers.
2. **Mobile App Development (mApp)** – Build native and cross-platform mobile applications using Swift, Kotlin, React Native, or Flutter.
3. **Web Design, UI/UX & Full-Stack Scripting** – From WordPress CMS to custom web scripting, frontend frameworks, and backend logic.
4. **Cloud Engineering & Web3 Architecture** – Deploy scalable cloud infrastructure (AWS/Azure) and build decentralized applications (dApps) using smart contracts.
5. **Computer-Aided Design (CAD) & 3D Graphics** – Professional 2D drafting and 3D parametric modeling for engineering and product design.
6. **Digital Media Production & Broadcasting** – End-to-end media workflows, multi-camera shooting, live broadcasting, and video editing.
7. **Data Analytics & Business Intelligence (BI)** – Transform raw data into strategic insights using SQL, Tableau/PowerBI, and analytical modeling.
8. **Digital Marketing, No-Code & Automation** – Build marketing funnels and automate workflows using no-code/low-code platforms (Zapier, Make).
9. **Data Engineering & Big Data Pipelines** – Architect robust ETL/ELT pipelines using Hadoop, Spark, Kafka, and data warehousing solutions.
10. **Machine Learning & Data Science** – Build predictive models and AI algorithms covering supervised/unsupervised learning, neural networks, and NLP.
11. **Game Development & Physics Simulations** – Create interactive simulations and games using Unity/Unreal, physics modeling, and real-time rendering.
12. **System Administration & Cybersecurity** – Secure enterprise networks, manage IT infrastructure, ethical hacking, threat modeling, and zero-trust architecture.
13. **Systems Engineering, Electronics, Robotics & IoT** – Bridge hardware and software: design embedded systems, program microcontrollers, and build IoT solutions.
14. **Geographic Information Systems (GIS) & Bioinformatics** – Analyze spatial data (ArcGIS/QGIS) and biological datasets for genomic and proteomic analysis.

