### STEM DOMAIN
1. **Applied Mathematics for Machine Learning & AI** – Deep dive into linear algebra, multivariate calculus, and optimization for neural networks.
2. **Engineering Mechanics, Kinematics & Physics Simulations** – Master classical mechanics, rigid body dynamics, and physics engine mathematics for CAD/Game Dev.
3. **Control Systems, Microcontrollers & Embedded Electronics** – Study PID controllers, sensor fusion, PCB design, and real-time embedded C/C++ programming.
4. **Spatial Data Science, Remote Sensing & GIS Analytics** – Master coordinate transformations, spatial statistics, LiDAR processing, and satellite imagery analysis.
5. **Computational Biology, Genomics & Proteomics** – Study sequence alignment algorithms, molecular modeling, and the application of ML to biological datasets.
6. **Advanced Statistics, Probability & Bayesian Inference** – Cover hypothesis testing, Markov chains, Bayesian networks, and time-series forecasting for Big Data.
7. **Discrete Mathematics, Cryptography & Graph Theory** – Master boolean logic, number theory, elliptic curve cryptography, and network graph algorithms for Web3/Dev.
8. **Materials Science, Metallurgy & Additive Manufacturing** – Study material properties, stress/strain analysis, and the science of 3D printing/sintering.
9. **Environmental Science, Ecology & Sustainability Eng.** – Study carbon cycle modeling, renewable energy thermodynamics, and environmental impact assessments.
10. **Fluid Dynamics, Thermodynamics & Heat Transfer** – Master Navier-Stokes equations, HVAC modeling, and thermal management in electronics.
11. **Neurobiology, Cognitive Science & Brain-Computer Interfaces** – Study neural pathways, synaptic plasticity, and the engineering of non-invasive BCI hardware.
12. **Operations Research, Linear Programming & Optimization** – Master the simplex method, queuing theory, and algorithmic optimization for logistics and data engineering.

